NorCal effectively improves baselines in diverse scenarios. We first apply NorCal to representative baselines for instance segmentation:
(1) Mask R-CNN <cit.> with feature pyramid networks <cit.>, which is trained with repeated factor sampling (RFS), following the standard training procedure in <cit.>;
(2) re-sampling/cost-sensitive based methods that have a multi-class classifier, e.g., cRT <cit.>;
(3) re-sampling/cost-sensitive based methods that have multiple binary classifiers, e.g., EQL <cit.>;
(4) data augmentation based methods, e.g., a state-of-the-art method MosaicOS <cit.>.
Please see the supplementary material for a comparison with other existing methods.

new_text:
NorCal improves baselines across diverse scenarios. We apply NorCal to representative instance segmentation baselines:  
(1) Mask R-CNN <cit.> with feature pyramid networks <cit.>, trained with repeated factor sampling (RFS) via the standard protocol <cit.>;  
(2) multi-class classifiers with re-sampling/cost-sensitive approaches, e.g., cRT <cit.>;  
(3) binary classifiers with re-sampling/cost-sensitive approaches, e.g., EQL <cit.>;  
(4) state-of-the-art data augmentation methods, e.g., MosaicOS <cit.>.  
A comprehensive comparison with other methods is provided in the supplementary material.

